Z||000000||200mph fierogt||08-12-2001||01:35 PM||||What is the best v6 swap? What is the best v6, and the lightest v6 that can go into a fiero gt? The engine with the best aftermarket parts?<P>And is there any good ways to make a fiero lighter?<BR>What part of that vehicle that makes it so heavy?<P>Thanx||||reg||5
Z||000001||Joe Torma||08-12-2001||02:47 PM||||The Fiero is so heavy because of the billion stamped steel parts for the spaceframe.<P>You may be starting a war asking what is the best V6 swap!<P>The lightest I guess is a BowTie Aluminum block 2.8/3.1  I don't think anyone has this though.  The most popular is the 3.8 Buick.  A nice setup too...some are supercharged!  <P>Then there are the 3.4s...most everyone who has this has the Camaro engine...same as 2.8 just more HP<P>There seems to be only one other person aside from me that has a 3400series engine.  I would say it is the second lightest setup.  It has a cast iron block with aluminum heads.  It has a serpintine belt and all the stuff on the front of the engine is compact...more so than the 2.8.  I should be making more power than stock SC 3.8s...desktop dyno says 300hp...I guess I'll see when I get it on the road.<P>I don't know how you can make the car lighter, aside from ditching a seat and the spare tire.<P>Joe<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 08-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||JayUSA77||08-12-2001||03:19 PM||||i just did a search from the forum and the v-6 according to people on the forum said it was around 360 pounds.i hope that helps.<BR>J <P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
